Index: debian-xymon/xymonnet/xymonnet.1
===================================================================
--- debian-xymon.orig/xymonnet/xymonnet.1
+++ debian-xymon/xymonnet/xymonnet.1
@@ -273,13 +273,25 @@ The default is "content".  If you have u
 scripts earlier, you may want to use "\-\-content=cont" to report content
 checks using the same test name as these scripts do.
 .IP \-\-bb\-proxy\-syntax
-Adhere to the Big Brother syntax for a URL, which allows specifying 
+Adhere to the Big Brother syntax for a URL, which allows specifying
 a HTTP proxy as part of a URL. See \fB"HTTP Testing via proxy"\fR in the
-.I hosts.cfg(5) 
+.I hosts.cfg(5)
 file for details. Beginning with Xymon 4.3.0, this behaviour is disabled
 by default since URL's that include other URL's are now much more
 common. This option restores the old Big Brother-compatible behaviour.
 
+.SH HTTP/2
+If xymonnet was built with the nghttp2 library, HTTP/2 is negotiated
+automatically for "https://" web tests using ALPN during the TLS
+handshake; servers that do not support HTTP/2 are tested over HTTP/1.1
+as before. HTTP/2 can be required with the "httpsh2://" scheme, or
+disabled per-test by pinning HTTP/1.x with "https11://". See
+.I hosts.cfg(5)
+for details. Cleartext HTTP/2 prior knowledge is available for direct tests
+with "httph2://"; HTTP/1.1 Upgrade and proxying are not supported. If xymonnet
+was built without nghttp2, HTTP/2 is not offered and required HTTP/2 tests
+report an error.
+
 .SH OPTIONS FOR SSL CERTIFICATE TESTS
 .IP \-\-ssl=SSLCERTTESTNAME
 Determines the name of the column Xymon displays for the SSL certificate checks.
